0:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 15.19, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": null, "poll_sd": null, "poll_weight": 0.0, "fundamentals": {"margin": 15.14, "lean": 4.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.94}, "rating_margin": 15.22, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.27, "baseline_margin": 15.19, "analyst_adjustment": -0.19, "key_factors": ["Incumbent Hillary Scholten has a 4-point partisan lean and strong fundraising edge ($2.3M vs $0.55M)", "All nine expert ratings put the race at Likely/Solid/Safe D", "Prediction markets price Scholten around 93-94%", "No public general-election polling, leaving some uncertainty"], "rationale": "The fundamentals favor Scholten: a Democratic-leaning district, incumbency, a large financial advantage, and no outside spending against her, while every expert rater and both prediction markets treat her as a heavy favorite. DeBoer's outsider primary win gives Republicans a credible nominee, but the evidence points to a comfortable incumbent margin.", "watch": "A late surge of outside spending against Scholten or new polling showing a much tighter race would warrant revisiting.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Hillary Scholten (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Hillary Scholten, the Democratic incumbent in west Michigan's 3rd District, seeks a third term against Republican Terri DeBoer, a former meteorologist who won an open primary as a political outsider. The district carries a modest Democratic lean, and Scholten has built a large financial advantage, raising $2.3 million to DeBoer's $550,000, with no outside groups opposing her so far.\n\nEvery major expert rating places the race in the Likely-to-Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets give Scholten roughly a 93-94% chance of winning. With no public general-election polling available, the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and markets, all of which point the same direction. DeBoer has drawn local coverage of her positions and party unity efforts, but the race remains a clear incumbent favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9846, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9771, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9798, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9738, "margin": 15.0}]}